IMPORT prelude

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), Part 7 Exercise of statutory functions: sections 46 to 49.
-- Whether an Act confers a power, and what a document says, are plain inputs.
-- A rule written "If an Act or instrument confers ..." answers JUST FALSE when the "if" fails, as the Guide rules for "if" conditions; a rule that says "includes" answers NOTHING outside its list.

§ `Part 7 Exercise of statutory functions`

§§ `46 Appointments may be made by name or by office`

-- How the person or body appoints, section 46(1).
DECLARE HowAnAppointmentIsMade IS ONE OF
    ByAppointingAPersonOrBodyByName
    ByAppointingAParticularOfficerOrTheHolderOfAParticularOfficeByTheTitleOfTheOffice
    ByAnotherMeansOfAppointing

-- src:522 | (1) If an Act or instrument confers a power on any person or body—
-- src:523 | (a) to appoint a person to an office,
-- src:524 | (b) to appoint a person or body to exercise a function, or
-- src:525 | (c) to appoint a person or body to do any other thing,
-- src:526 | the person or body may make the appointment by appointing a person or body by name or by appointing a particular officer or the holder of a particular office by reference to the title of the office concerned.
@ref s 46(1) (src:522-526)
GIVEN `an Act or instrument confers a power on a person or body to appoint a person to an office, to appoint a person or body to exercise a function, or to appoint a person or body to do any other thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      how IS A HowAnAppointmentIsMade
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(1) the person or body may make the appointment in that way` MEANS
    IF `an Act or instrument confers a power on a person or body to appoint a person to an office, to appoint a person or body to exercise a function, or to appoint a person or body to do any other thing`
    THEN CONSIDER how
         WHEN ByAppointingAPersonOrBodyByName THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN ByAppointingAParticularOfficerOrTheHolderOfAParticularOfficeByTheTitleOfTheOffice THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN ByAnotherMeansOfAppointing THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:527 | (2) Any appointment of a particular officer or the holder of a particular office shall be taken to be the appointment of the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned.
@ref s 46(2) (src:527)
GIVEN `it is an appointment of a particular officer or the holder of a particular office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(2) the appointment is taken to be the appointment of the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned` MEANS
    IF `it is an appointment of a particular officer or the holder of a particular office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `47 Powers of appointment imply certain incidental powers`

-- src:530 | (1) If an Act or instrument confers a power on any person or body to appoint a person to an office—
-- src:531 | (a) the power may be exercised from time to time, as occasion requires, and
@ref s 47(1)(a) (src:530-531)
GIVEN `an Act or instrument confers a power on a person or body to appoint a person to an office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(1)(a) the power may be exercised from time to time, as occasion requires` MEANS
    IF `an Act or instrument confers a power on a person or body to appoint a person to an office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The incidental powers section 47(1)(b) names. "includes" leaves the list open.
DECLARE IncidentalPowerOfAppointment IS ONE OF
    PowerToRemoveOrSuspendAtAnyTimeAPersonSoAppointed
    PowerToAppointSomeOtherPersonToActInTheOfficeOfAPersonSoRemovedOrSuspended
    PowerToAppointAPersonToActInAVacantOffice
    PowerToAppointAPersonToActInTheOfficeOfAPersonWhoIsAbsent
    SomeOtherIncidentalPower

-- src:530 | (1) If an Act or instrument confers a power on any person or body to appoint a person to an office—
-- src:531 | (a) the power may be exercised from time to time, as occasion requires, and
-- src:532 | (b) the power includes—
-- src:533 | (i) power to remove or suspend, at any time, a person so appointed,
-- src:534 | (ii) power to appoint some other person to act in the office of a person so removed or suspended,
-- src:535 | (iii) power to appoint a person to act in a vacant office, whether or not the office has ever been filled, and
-- src:536 | (iv) power to appoint a person to act in the office of a person who is absent from that office, whether because of illness or otherwise.
@ref s 47(1)(b) (src:530-536)
GIVEN `an Act or instrument confers a power on a person or body to appoint a person to an office` IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A IncidentalPowerOfAppointment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(1)(b) the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power` MEANS
    IF `an Act or instrument confers a power on a person or body to appoint a person to an office`
    THEN CONSIDER power
         WHEN PowerToRemoveOrSuspendAtAnyTimeAPersonSoAppointed THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN PowerToAppointSomeOtherPersonToActInTheOfficeOfAPersonSoRemovedOrSuspended THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN PowerToAppointAPersonToActInAVacantOffice THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN PowerToAppointAPersonToActInTheOfficeOfAPersonWhoIsAbsent THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN SomeOtherIncidentalPower THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:537 | (2) The power to remove or suspend a person under subsection (1) (b) may be exercised even if the Act or instrument under which the person was appointed provides that a holder of the office to which the person was appointed shall hold office for a specified period of time.
@ref s 47(2) (src:537)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument under which the person was appointed provides that a holder of the office shall hold office for a specified period of time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(2) the power to remove or suspend the person may be exercised` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument under which the person was appointed provides that a holder of the office shall hold office for a specified period of time` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- The ways section 47(3) says the power to make an appointment may be exercised.
DECLARE WayOfExercisingThePowerToAppoint IS ONE OF
    AsOccasionRequires
    InAnticipationOfAParticularEventSoThatTheAppointmentTakesEffectWhenItOccurs
    InAnticipationOfAParticularStateOfAffairsSoThatTheAppointmentHasEffectWhileItExists
    InSomeOtherWay

-- src:538 | (3) The power to make an appointment under subsection (1) (b) may be exercised—
-- src:539 | (a) as occasion requires,
-- src:540 | (b) in anticipation of a particular event, so as to provide that the appointment shall take effect when that event occurs, or
-- src:541 | (c) in anticipation of a particular state of affairs, so as to provide that the appointment shall have effect while that state of affairs exists.
@ref s 47(3) (src:538-541)
GIVEN way IS A WayOfExercisingThePowerToAppoint
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(3) the power to make an appointment under section 47(1)(b) may be exercised in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN AsOccasionRequires THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN InAnticipationOfAParticularEventSoThatTheAppointmentTakesEffectWhenItOccurs THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN InAnticipationOfAParticularStateOfAffairsSoThatTheAppointmentHasEffectWhileItExists THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN InSomeOtherWay THEN NOTHING

§§ `48 Exercise of statutory functions`

-- src:544 | (1) If an Act or instrument confers or imposes a function on any person or body, the function may be exercised (or, in the case of a duty, shall be performed) from time to time as occasion requires.
@ref s 48(1) (src:544)
GIVEN `an Act or instrument confers or imposes a function on a person or body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(1) the function may be exercised, or in the case of a duty shall be performed, from time to time as occasion requires` MEANS
    IF `an Act or instrument confers or imposes a function on a person or body` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:545 | (2) If an Act or instrument confers or imposes a function on a particular officer or the holder of a particular office, the function may be exercised (or, in the case of a duty, shall be performed) by the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned.
@ref s 48(2) (src:545)
GIVEN `an Act or instrument confers or imposes a function on a particular officer or the holder of a particular office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(2) the function may be exercised, or in the case of a duty shall be performed, by the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned` MEANS
    IF `an Act or instrument confers or imposes a function on a particular officer or the holder of a particular office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `49 Delegation of functions`

-- How the delegate is described, section 49(1).
DECLARE HowTheDelegateIsDescribed IS ONE OF
    ByNameAsAPersonOrBody
    AsAParticularOfficerOrTheHolderOfAParticularOfficeByTheTitleOfTheOffice
    InSomeOtherWay49

-- src:548 | (1) If an Act or instrument confers a power on any person or body to delegate a function, the person or body may, in accordance with the Act or instrument, delegate the function to a person or body by name or to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office by reference to the title of the office concerned.
@ref s 49(1) (src:548)
GIVEN `an Act or instrument confers a power on a person or body to delegate a function` IS A BOOLEAN
      described IS A HowTheDelegateIsDescribed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(1) the person or body may, in accordance with the Act or instrument, delegate the function to the delegate so described` MEANS
    IF `an Act or instrument confers a power on a person or body to delegate a function`
    THEN CONSIDER described
         WHEN ByNameAsAPersonOrBody THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN AsAParticularOfficerOrTheHolderOfAParticularOfficeByTheTitleOfTheOffice THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN InSomeOtherWay49 THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The scope of a delegation, section 49(2)(a).
DECLARE ScopeOfADelegation IS ONE OF
    AGeneralDelegation
    ALimitedDelegation
    SomeOtherScopeOfDelegation

-- src:549 | (2) A delegation—
-- src:550 | (a) may be general or limited,
@ref s 49(2)(a) (src:549-550)
GIVEN scope IS A ScopeOfADelegation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(2)(a) a delegation may be of that scope` MEANS
    CONSIDER scope
    WHEN AGeneralDelegation THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN ALimitedDelegation THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN SomeOtherScopeOfDelegation THEN NOTHING

-- src:549 | (2) A delegation—
-- src:550 | (a) may be general or limited,
-- src:551 | (b) shall be in, or be evidenced by, writing signed by the delegator or, if the delegator is a body, by a person authorised by the body for that purpose, and
@ref s 49(2)(b) (src:549-551)
GIVEN `the delegation is in, or is evidenced by, writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegator is a body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing is signed by the delegator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the writing is signed by a person authorised by the body for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 49(2)(b) the delegation is in, or is evidenced by, writing signed as the section requires` MEANS
    `the delegation is in, or is evidenced by, writing`
    AND (IF `the delegator is a body` THEN `the writing is signed by a person authorised by the body for that purpose` ELSE `the writing is signed by the delegator`)

-- src:549 | (2) A delegation—
-- src:550 | (a) may be general or limited,
-- src:551 | (b) shall be in, or be evidenced by, writing signed by the delegator or, if the delegator is a body, by a person authorised by the body for that purpose, and
-- src:552 | (c) may be revoked, wholly or partly, by the delegator.
@ref s 49(2)(c) (src:549-552)
GIVEN `the revocation is by the delegator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(2)(c) the delegation may be revoked, wholly or partly` MEANS
    IF `the revocation is by the delegator` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:553 | (3) A delegated function may be exercised only in accordance with any conditions to which the delegation is subject.
@ref s 49(3) (src:553)
GIVEN `the exercise is in accordance with any conditions to which the delegation is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(3) the delegated function may be exercised` MEANS
    IF `the exercise is in accordance with any conditions to which the delegation is subject` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:554 | (4) A delegate may, in the exercise of a delegated function, exercise any other function that is incidental to the delegated function.
@ref s 49(4) (src:554)
GIVEN `the other function is incidental to the delegated function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(4) the delegate may, in the exercise of the delegated function, exercise the other function` MEANS
    IF `the other function is incidental to the delegated function` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:555 | (5) A delegated function that purports to have been exercised by a delegate shall, until the contrary is proved, be taken to have been duly exercised by the delegate.
@ref s 49(5) (src:555)
GIVEN `a delegated function purports to have been exercised by a delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(5) the delegated function is taken to have been duly exercised by the delegate` MEANS
    IF `a delegated function purports to have been exercised by a delegate` THEN JUST (NOT `the contrary is proved`) ELSE NOTHING

-- src:556 | (6) A delegated function that is duly exercised by a delegate shall be taken to have been exercised by the delegator.
@ref s 49(6) (src:556)
GIVEN `a delegated function is duly exercised by a delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(6) the delegated function is taken to have been exercised by the delegator` MEANS
    IF `a delegated function is duly exercised by a delegate` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:557 | (7) If—
-- src:558 | (a) the exercise of a function by a person or body is, by virtue of an Act or instrument, dependent on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the person or body in relation to any matter, and
-- src:559 | (b) the person or body has delegated the function to some other person or body,
-- src:560 | the function may be exercised by the delegate on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the delegate in relation to any such matter.
@ref s 49(7) (src:557-560)
GIVEN `the exercise of the function is, by virtue of an Act or instrument, dependent on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the person or body in relation to a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or body has delegated the function to some other person or body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(7) the function may be exercised by the delegate on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the delegate in relation to the matter` MEANS
    IF `the exercise of the function is, by virtue of an Act or instrument, dependent on the opinion, belief or state of mind of the person or body in relation to a matter` AND `the person or body has delegated the function to some other person or body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:561 | (8) If a function is delegated by or to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office—
-- src:562 | (a) the delegation does not cease to have effect merely because the person who was the particular officer or the holder of the particular office when the function was delegated ceases to be that officer or the holder of that office, and
@ref s 49(8)(a) (src:561-562)
GIVEN `a function is delegated by or to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who was the particular officer or the holder of the office when the function was delegated ceases to be that officer or the holder of that office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(8)(a) the delegation ceases to have effect merely because the person ceases to be that officer or the holder of that office` MEANS
    IF `a function is delegated by or to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office` AND `the person who was the particular officer or the holder of the office when the function was delegated ceases to be that officer or the holder of that office`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:561 | (8) If a function is delegated by or to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office—
-- src:562 | (a) the delegation does not cease to have effect merely because the person who was the particular officer or the holder of the particular office when the function was delegated ceases to be that officer or the holder of that office, and
-- src:563 | (b) the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned is taken to be the delegator or delegate (as the case requires).
@ref s 49(8)(b) (src:561-563)
GIVEN `a function is delegated by or to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(8)(b) the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned is taken to be the delegator or delegate` MEANS
    IF `a function is delegated by or to a particular officer or the holder of a particular office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:564 | (9) A function that has been delegated may, notwithstanding the delegation, be exercised by the delegator.
@ref s 49(9) (src:564)
GIVEN `the function has been delegated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(9) the function may, notwithstanding the delegation, be exercised by the delegator` MEANS
    IF `the function has been delegated` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:565 | (10) This section applies to a sub-delegation of a function in the same way as it applies to a delegation of a function, but only in so far as the Act or instrument that authorises the delegation of the function also authorises the sub-delegation of the function.
@ref s 49(10) (src:565)
GIVEN `it is a sub-delegation of a function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act or instrument that authorises the delegation of the function also authorises the sub-delegation of the function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(10) section 49 applies to the sub-delegation in the same way as it applies to a delegation` MEANS
    IF `it is a sub-delegation of a function`
    THEN JUST `the Act or instrument that authorises the delegation of the function also authorises the sub-delegation of the function`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Tests: Part 7`

-- s 46
#ASSERT `s 46(1) the person or body may make the appointment in that way` TRUE ByAppointingAPersonOrBodyByName EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46(1) the person or body may make the appointment in that way` TRUE ByAppointingAParticularOfficerOrTheHolderOfAParticularOfficeByTheTitleOfTheOffice EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46(1) the person or body may make the appointment in that way` TRUE ByAnotherMeansOfAppointing EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 46(1) the person or body may make the appointment in that way` FALSE ByAppointingAPersonOrBodyByName EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46(2) the appointment is taken to be the appointment of the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 46(2) the appointment is taken to be the appointment of the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 47
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(a) the power may be exercised from time to time, as occasion requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(a) the power may be exercised from time to time, as occasion requires` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(b) the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power` TRUE PowerToRemoveOrSuspendAtAnyTimeAPersonSoAppointed EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(b) the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power` TRUE PowerToAppointSomeOtherPersonToActInTheOfficeOfAPersonSoRemovedOrSuspended EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(b) the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power` TRUE PowerToAppointAPersonToActInAVacantOffice EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(b) the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power` TRUE PowerToAppointAPersonToActInTheOfficeOfAPersonWhoIsAbsent EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(b) the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power` TRUE SomeOtherIncidentalPower EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(1)(b) the power to appoint a person to an office includes the power` FALSE PowerToAppointAPersonToActInAVacantOffice EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the power to remove or suspend the person may be exercised` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the power to remove or suspend the person may be exercised` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(3) the power to make an appointment under section 47(1)(b) may be exercised in that way` AsOccasionRequires EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(3) the power to make an appointment under section 47(1)(b) may be exercised in that way` InAnticipationOfAParticularEventSoThatTheAppointmentTakesEffectWhenItOccurs EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(3) the power to make an appointment under section 47(1)(b) may be exercised in that way` InAnticipationOfAParticularStateOfAffairsSoThatTheAppointmentHasEffectWhileItExists EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(3) the power to make an appointment under section 47(1)(b) may be exercised in that way` InSomeOtherWay EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 48
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the function may be exercised, or in the case of a duty shall be performed, from time to time as occasion requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the function may be exercised, or in the case of a duty shall be performed, from time to time as occasion requires` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(2) the function may be exercised, or in the case of a duty shall be performed, by the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(2) the function may be exercised, or in the case of a duty shall be performed, by the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 49
#ASSERT `s 49(1) the person or body may, in accordance with the Act or instrument, delegate the function to the delegate so described` TRUE ByNameAsAPersonOrBody EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(1) the person or body may, in accordance with the Act or instrument, delegate the function to the delegate so described` TRUE AsAParticularOfficerOrTheHolderOfAParticularOfficeByTheTitleOfTheOffice EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(1) the person or body may, in accordance with the Act or instrument, delegate the function to the delegate so described` TRUE InSomeOtherWay49 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 49(1) the person or body may, in accordance with the Act or instrument, delegate the function to the delegate so described` FALSE ByNameAsAPersonOrBody EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 49(2)(a) a delegation may be of that scope` AGeneralDelegation EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(2)(a) a delegation may be of that scope` ALimitedDelegation EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(2)(a) a delegation may be of that scope` SomeOtherScopeOfDelegation EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 49(2)(b) the delegation is in, or is evidenced by, writing signed as the section requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(2)(b) the delegation is in, or is evidenced by, writing signed as the section requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(2)(b) the delegation is in, or is evidenced by, writing signed as the section requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 49(2)(b) the delegation is in, or is evidenced by, writing signed as the section requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 49(2)(b) the delegation is in, or is evidenced by, writing signed as the section requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 49(2)(c) the delegation may be revoked, wholly or partly` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49(2)(c) the delegation may be revoked, wholly or partly` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
